# Every text file is committed with LF and checked out with LF on every platform,
# whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine. On 2026-09-28 a tool flipped 83 tracked
# files to CRLF in one sitting, which would have buried a Makefile change under
# seventeen thousand whitespace lines and left the python shebang ending in "\r".
# .editorconfig says the same thing to editors; this says it to git.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Written by Visual Studio and NuGet on Windows, always with CRLF, and read back by
# the same tools. Left as they are written rather than fought over.
*.pubxml -text
packages.lock.json -text
